 ## Manual gameplay checks
 
+`host_tests --render-pass-gpu` checks real attachment clear/load operations,
+two color attachments, depth and framebuffer resource lifetime through readback.
+Run it and `host_tests --presenter-gpu` with
+`RECOMP_VULKAN_LEGACY_RENDER_PASSES=1` to verify the fallback on a Vulkan device
+that also supports dynamic rendering. `RECOMP_GPU_VALIDATE=1` requests validation
+layers and reports explicitly when none are available.
+
+`RECOMP_HOST_SECONDS=10` requests a normal guest close after ten seconds in the
+SDL desktop app, for bounded startup/display/audio diagnostics. Invalid or
+nonpositive values leave the normal run unlimited. Combine this with
+`RECOMP_HOST_AUDIO_CAPTURE=/private/path.wav` to inspect mixer output. A completed
+startup diagnostic does not verify physical input or later gameplay.
